# 9. Source `/etc/os-release`

Your script uses:

```bash
. /etc/os-release
```

This loads OS information into the current shell.

Then:

```bash
echo "$PRETTY_NAME"
```

might produce:

```text
Ubuntu 24.04 LTS
```

Other useful variables include:

```bash
echo "$NAME"
echo "$VERSION"
echo "$VERSION_ID"
echo "$PRETTY_NAME"
```

Very useful when writing scripts that need to behave differently on different Linux distributions.

