# 11. Redirect Errors

Your script uses:

```bash
2>/dev/null
```

This means:

```text
2      → stderr
>      → redirect
/dev/null → discard output
```

Example:

```bash
du -xhd 1 / 2>/dev/null
```

This prevents permission-denied messages from cluttering the output.

---

# 12. Pipes ⭐

```bash
command1 | command2
```

Example:

```bash
ps aux | grep nginx
```

Another:

```bash
du -sh /var/* | sort -hr | head
```

The output of one command becomes the input of the next.

---

# 13. Error Handling Pattern

A useful pattern:

```bash
if command; then
    echo "Command successful"
else
    echo "Command failed"
    exit 1
fi
```

Example:

```bash
if systemctl restart nginx; then
    echo "Nginx restarted successfully"
else
    echo "Failed to restart Nginx"
    exit 1
fi
```

